Adapted elements: equipment frame layout and checksum; ReadWriteData section
bitmap layout; status, command, device and WorkoutMode code tables; converter
names and access flags for the bike field subset; DeviceInfo / SystemInfo /
VersionInfo identity offsets; the part-number fix-up; the VerifySecurity
payload layout; the 32-byte security-hash algorithm; and the unlock retry
spacing used as a default reauthentication policy. Fixtures in
src/test/kotlin/.../Fixtures.kt labelled STRIDE_* are quoted byte sequences
from protocol/FITPRO_PROTOCOL.md.

Changes made by Fitbaus (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)): the code is a new Kotlin
implementation rather than a copy of STRIDE source files. It restricts the
command set to a read-only/authentication allowlist; removes all treadmill
speed/grade/fan fields and every write path from the public API; adds strict
frame, length, device, command and status validation; reports sentinel and
invalid values per field; implements a Fitbaus-owned resistance codec from
F2.3 physical samples rather than leaving encoding unresolved; uses Int32
arithmetic right-shift on the security-hash part operand to match the locally
observed Legacy helper (STRIDE's published mix uses unsigned shifts); adds a
bounded reauthentication state machine; and contains no USB, Android, or
network I/O.

